# The conditional answer {isGroup: true}

[only-if-outweighed]: It is permissible to interfere in the transformative choices of others only if their right to revelatory autonomy is outweighed. #core
    {fidelity: "quotation", pinpoint: "p. 9",
     source: "\"it is permissible to interfere in the transformative choices of others *only if* their right to revelatory autonomy is outweighed\""}

[outweighed-then-permissible]: If someone's right to revelatory autonomy is outweighed and our duty of non-interference no longer binds us, then it is permissible to interfere to try to prevent them from making that transformative choice. #core
    {fidelity: "paraphrase", pinpoint: "p. 9",
     source: "\"then it is permissible to interfere to try to prevent another from making some transformative choice\"",
     note: "The author marks this as a further suggestion, not something derived from the right and the duty: 'I suggest further that...'."}

[conditional-answer]: Interference in another's transformative choice is permissible when, and only when, that person's right to revelatory autonomy is outweighed. #core
    {fidelity: "compression", pinpoint: "p. 9",
     note: "A join, and worth marking: the 'only if' half and the 'if' half are stated in successive sentences and the author never conjoins them himself, so the biconditional is the reconstruction's. The second half is also offered with less confidence than the first -- 'I suggest further that' -- and the phrasing of the whole reaches back to The Question on p. 4."}

[necessary-condition-on-all-interference]: The right to revelatory autonomy places a necessary condition on every form of interference alike. #core
    {fidelity: "paraphrase", pinpoint: "p. 5",
     source: "\"the distinctive moral right we possess concerning transformative choices places a necessary condition on all such interference\""}

<Conditional Answer>: The right and its correlative duty give the necessary condition; a further suggestion of the author's gives the sufficient one. #core
    {fidelity: "interpretation", warrant: "coherence"}

